## Why here, specifically

Other places have saunas. What this one has is the creek immediately outside the door, and the particular quality of quiet that comes with a tidal waterway in the Northern Neck. There is no marina noise, no traffic. If you want to know what the stretch of water around Heathsville feels like at this remove from everything, the <a href={withBase("/area")}>area page</a> has more on the geography — but the honest version is that you have to be in the sauna, looking west at the water, to understand why the ritual works here and not somewhere else.

{/* TODO: Will to confirm — sauna capacity: how many guests fit? 2-person? 4-person? */}

The kayaks and the paddleboard wait on the bank. The kettlebells are in the shed. There is more than enough to do at the <a href={withBase("/activities")}>activities page</a>, but the sauna sequence is the one I find myself thinking about most between visits — the one that makes the trip feel like a repair rather than just a break.

